    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1168">

                <pb facs="1103" n="1091" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg1091"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">819.00/1990: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dawson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-02-20T17:00:00-05:00">February 20, 1940—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>14. Your despatch No. 307, February 12.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d1168-f1"/> This
                    Government is determined by policy and bound by treaty not to intervene directly
                    or indirectly in the internal affairs of Panama. Therefore, the supervision of
                    the forthcoming elections or the disarmament of the national police in
                    connection with those elections are out of the question.</p>
                <p>The Department agrees with you that no reply need be made to the communication
                    which you have already received or to others which you may receive in the
                    future.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1168-f1" n="27" xml:id="d1168-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed. The Ambassador transmitted a communication from supporters of a
                    Panamanian presidential candidate requesting that the United States disarm the
                    National Police and supervise the elections to be held on June 2, 1940, to
                    insure fair elections.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
